    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-07",
      "edition": "Saturday 7 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Jack Crowley injured, handing Sam Prendergast another shot at No. 10 against Argentina",
          "body": "Farrell announced his team on Wednesday, and the number 10 berth is now open to Sam Prendergast while Crowley is sidelined by injury. Prendergast made his debut in this fixture two years ago, aged 21, and BBC Sport describes his Test career as uneven. Argentina have never beaten Ireland in Dublin, though they have won all three of their World Cup meetings. Ireland have won 14 of the 20 meetings between the sides."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England captain Itoje returns; Fin Smith starts at fly-half",
          "body": "South Africa's Kolbe out injured; Hooker named on wing. France set to reunite Dupont and Ntamack at half-back."
