      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "League approach",
          "heading": "Bill Sweeney confirms WRU's formal approach to join Anglo-Welsh league",
          "body": "Sweeney told BBC Radio Four the RFU has received a formal approach from the WRU asking to be part of an Anglo-Welsh tournament. The WRU has plans to cut one of its four professional sides, Ospreys, Cardiff, Scarlets or Dragons, which currently play in the 16-team United Rugby Championship. Sweeney said the English game remains the primary focus, and no formal talks have yet taken place with the Welsh side. The Prem hopes to grow from 10 to 12 teams for the 2029-30 season."
        },
